---
import Site from "../layouts/Site.astro";
---

<Site
  title="Your information"
  description="How After Hours Agenda handles support requests, email consent, saved pieces, order lookup and optional aggregate website measurement."
>
  <header class="page-head shell">
    <p class="label">Website information / October 9, 2026</p>
    <h1>
      YOUR
      <br />
      <span class="accent">INFORMATION.</span>
    </h1>
    <p class="lede">
      A clear account of what this website does with your details.
    </p>
  </header>
  <article class="reading shell">
    <section>
      <h2>Support and returns</h2>
      <p>
        When you submit a form, the details are stored with our website host,
        Netlify, so we can answer your request. Support does not subscribe you
        to marketing. Do not send card numbers, passwords or sensitive
        information. Email and carrier services use their own privacy practices.
      </p>
    </section>
    <section>
      <h2>Email updates</h2>
      <p>
        The signup form records your email, optional interests, your explicit
        consent and the version of the notice. You can{" "}
        <a href="/unsubscribe/">unsubscribe here</a> or email
        info@afterhoursagenda.com. Marketing is separate from necessary messages
        about an existing order.
      </p>
    </section>
    <section>
      <h2>Saved pieces and bag</h2>
      <p>
        Your saved items and bag are stored on your device when storage is
        available. They contain product identifiers and quantities, not contact
        or payment details. Clearing website data removes them. They do not
        reserve stock.
      </p>
    </section>
    <section>
      <h2>Order lookup</h2>
      <p>
        The order tool checks the order number, checkout email and shipping
        postal code against existing records. It returns only customer-facing
        progress, item details and safe tracking links. It does not expose the
        stored address or payment-card data. Entries are not added to analytics.
      </p>
    </section>
    <section id="choices">
      <h2>Measurement is optional</h2>
      <div>
        <p>
          With your permission, we count page views and actions such as a
          successful signup, and measure loading speed, interaction
          responsiveness and layout shifts. The event payload excludes your
          email, order information, search terms, full URLs, advertising
          identifiers and IP address. The host still receives technical request
          information needed to serve and secure the website.
        </p>
        <p>
          We store daily aggregate counts and performance buckets, not browsing
          profiles. No advertising trackers are loaded. Global Privacy Control
          and Do Not Track disable this collection.
        </p>
        <div class="actions">
          <button type="button" class="button" data-privacy="allow">
            Allow measurement
          </button>
          <button
            type="button"
            class="button button-secondary"
            data-privacy="deny"
          >
            Keep measurement off
          </button>
        </div>
        <p data-privacy-status role="status"></p>
      </div>
    </section>
    <section>
      <h2>Questions and requests</h2>
      <p>
        For access, correction, deletion or a privacy question, write to{" "}
        <a href="mailto:info@afterhoursagenda.com">info@afterhoursagenda.com</a>
        . Existing purchase and privacy obligations remain in force. Reviews of
        this website never access or change customer records.
      </p>
    </section>
  </article>
</Site>
